      ],
      "year": 2020,
      "abstract": "Abstract Many recent commentators have noticed how Adorno, in his late works, borrows Kant\u2019s definition of enlightenment to define key areas of his own critical practice. These discussions, however, have failed to notice how these late borrowings present an image of Kant\u2019s enlightenment which is diametrically opposed to his previous discussions. By tracing the development of Adorno\u2019s engagement with Kant\u2019s essay, I discover Adorno deliberately sublating Kant\u2019s definition as to enable its incorporation into his own works. Further, the article will examine some problems which appear to arise for Adorno when borrowing Kant\u2019s definition of enlightenment in his late works, which coalesce around the topics of negativism and the prospects for societal change.",
